4"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T21:59:57-07:00","id":1067402,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1066792-dark-eras-fall-of-isireion-discussion?p=1067389#post1067389\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Finally made it through the chapter. Excellent read. I'm going to have to take another look at Immortals now to brush up on how each type is supposed to work.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm a little sad that the Reborn never got mechanics, but at least it lets me feel like my Incarnates aren't wasted.<br /> <br /> Were the Visitors in the original Immortals book? I don't really remember.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T22:39:50-07:00","id":1067417,"title":"","content":"Yes, they believed they were aliens.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T23:59:45-07:00","id":1067429,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1066792-dark-eras-fall-of-isireion-discussion?p=1067402#post1067402\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm a little sad that the Reborn never got mechanics, but at least it lets me feel like my Incarnates aren't wasted.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like the Era's take on the Reborn but I also like the idea that they're allies to the Deathless. If Imhotep is Deathless then I think of the Reborn as Anck-sun-amun, from the Mummy movies","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-24T00:21:49-07:00","id":1067435,"title":"","content":"I'm leaning towards this being the best release so far for Mummy. There's so much in it!! The writers and developer have pulled out all the stops, so thank you so much <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/164-malcolm\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar164_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"164\" data-vbnamecard=\"164\">Malcolm</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/152-the-gentleman-gamer\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar152_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"152\" data-vbnamecard=\"152\">The Gentleman Gamer</a>, and of course <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar638_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"638\" data-vbnamecard=\"638\">reseru</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3241-stannis","name":"Stannis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3241_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"115"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-24T05:12:45-07:00","id":1067507,"title":"","content":"To expand on the above point, I've realized the books I love by OPP (Sothis Ascends, Tome of Secrets, this one, others) always have Dawkins and / or Sheppard on them. They seem to excel at packing content into their books. This book gives us sorcerers, new antagonists, new relics, a new magic system, history, chronicle ideas, cults, more Deceived, and much more. It's ridiculously good.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3241-stannis","name":"Stannis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3241_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"115"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-24T05:29:23-07:00","id":1067514,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Azahul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1066792-dark-eras-fall-of-isireion-discussion?p=1067303#post1067303\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Rite of Seeding does strike me as a pretty efficient way of building up a cult over a few generations, but only if you've got Arisen backing.<br /> <br /> What weirds me out is that it basically replicates a Tier 3 Utterance, which is something Rites aren't meant to do. Sure, Seeds of Life is pretty much at the bottom end of the scale when it comes to Utterances, and it doesn't copy 100% of the functionality, but it does do some cool extra little bits (like the Presence boost).</div> </div> </div> </div>Rites aren't suppose to do that <b><i>anymore</i></b>. Remember, they used to be more powerful. They might not qualify as a template (or even a Hurt Locker style merit template) anymore, but it does hint they used to be a lot stronger. Especially the ones trained by the Nameless Empire. Of course, you have to be alive to learn and/or use it.<br /> <br /> I also love how they mention how the Immortals are tied to Cults. I can see more than one taking up with a sorcerous society.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-24T05:48:35-07:00","id":1067522,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1066792-dark-eras-fall-of-isireion-discussion?p=1067514#post1067514\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Rites aren't suppose to do that <b><i>anymore</i></b>. Remember, they used to be more powerful. They might not qualify as a template (or even a Hurt Locker style merit template) anymore, but it does hint they used to be a lot stronger. Especially the ones trained by the Nameless Empire. Of course, you have to be alive to learn and/or use it.</div> </div> </div> </div>...sure. That doesn't explain why this one is still that powerful, given all the stuff about how they aren't meant to be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-24T06:12:31-07:00","id":1067531,"title":"","content":"Reinforcement; they see it being done, it is well documented and you can just summon up one it's early adopters (if not innovaters) to fill you in on how it is supposed to work. The fact that it is an Utterance makes it easier to retain, particularly given I can see the Arisen delegating the job if they can.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-24T06:40:36-07:00","id":1067542,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1066792-dark-eras-fall-of-isireion-discussion?p=1067531#post1067531\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Reinforcement; they see it being done, it is well documented and you can just summon up one it's early adopters (if not innovaters) to fill you in on how it is supposed to work. The fact that it is an Utterance makes it easier to retain, particularly given I can see the Arisen delegating the job if they can.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok. So why don't Rites let you hurl meteors? Or any other high tier Utterance effect?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-24T07:00:19-07:00","id":1067551,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1066792-dark-eras-fall-of-isireion-discussion?p=1067402#post1067402\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm a little sad that the Reborn never got mechanics, but at least it lets me feel like my Incarnates aren't wasted.<br /> <br /> Were the Visitors in the original Immortals book? I don't really remember.</div> </div> </div> </div> The visitors in Immortals were quite different.<br /> <br /> They were the result of some spirits getting hit by atomic testing and it mutated them into physical beings that live in human brains, can learn a couple of numina like say telepathy or telekinesis, and reproduce by drilling out of their hosts skull, which has a good chance of killing the character. <br /> <br /> Interesting idea, but doesn't offer a lot of options. <br /> <br /> I suppose if one wanted use the existing systems for them and incorporate this &quot;We're from outer space, really!&quot; aspect here, one could give them access to that &quot;make alien technology&quot; numina the Greys have in Summoners, if memory serves.<br /> '<br /> Which would allow them to macguyver &quot;alien technology&quot; which sounds a whole lot of fun to me. <br /> <br /> &quot;I have a ray gun and I'm not afraid to use it!&quot; <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-24T13:07:08-07:00","id":1067753,"title":"","content":"I liked the chapter. I had a derp moment though, when I read the Legio sidebar on pg. 43, reading the quote in the voice of Curly Howard from the Three Stooges. Don't ask me why! ^_^;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-04T09:17:31-07:00","id":1073169,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrParaduo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1066792-dark-eras-fall-of-isireion-discussion?p=1067753#post1067753\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I liked the chapter. I had a derp moment though, when I read the Legio sidebar on pg. 43, reading the quote in the voice of Curly Howard from the Three Stooges. Don't ask me why! ^_^;</div> </div> </div> </div>What did you think of the Legio as an antagonist?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#000080\">Matthew Dawkins</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000080\">In-House Developer for Onyx Path Publishing</span></b><br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#008080\">Website: </span><a href=\"http://www.matthewdawkins.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.matthewdawkins.com</span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">Patreon: </span><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins</span></a></b></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/152-the-gentleman-gamer","name":"The Gentleman Gamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-04T10:31:07-07:00","id":1073236,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Gentleman Gamer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1066792-dark-eras-fall-of-isireion-discussion?p=1073169#post1073169\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What did you think of the Legio as an antagonist?</div> </div> </div> </div>An interesting reminder of humility among the deathless, and a potential clue to the reality of their masters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-05T03:40:15-07:00","id":1073653,"title":"","content":"I like the Legio because, along with a couple other reasons, they portray the horrifying scale that the Rite of Return encompassed. This was also established with the Book of the Deceived, IIRC, where some passages could be read implying the Rite more or less totally <i>fucked</i> time.<br /> <br /> It's not just sacrificed Shuankhsen, betrayed Deceived, or chosen Arisen that were affected by the Rite, but the realm of ghosts, and who knows what else. Its unintended consequences were just as influential as its intended designs","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-14T11:37:54-07:00","id":1092399,"title":"","content":"I have a question about Open Rites and Open Rite Mastery:<br /> <br /> Do you buy Open Rite Mastery for <i>each </i>open rite or once bought it applies to every open rite you can perform?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-18T22:29:40-07:00","id":1094428,"title":"","content":"So Visitors are the diet version of the Great Race?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3670-spook359","name":"Spook359","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3670_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-07T09:49:13-08:00","id":1183288,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1066792-dark-eras-fall-of-isireion-discussion?p=1066917#post1066917\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm only at the Cult of Isis, but so far this has more than redeemed Mummy's Dark Eras content. All the beats that I felt like were missed opportunities in Ruins of Empire are being hit squarely here, and it's tying in multiple eras to boot. So far I'm seeing To the Strongest, Requiem for Rome, and The Cannibal Hymn, but I'm likely missing some too. Hell, the Requiem tie-ins aren't even by dint of occupying the same time periods, I'm pretty sure I saw the Legio Mortuum explicitly referenced when I did my initial skim! This is awesome.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm curious about the ties the era have to those other Eras, specially To the Strongest. Can you (or someone else) help me out? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/196-max-deltree","name":"Max Deltree","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar196_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"178"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-07T12:55:34-08:00","id":1183356,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Max Deltree</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1066792-dark-eras-fall-of-isireion-discussion?p=1183288#post1183288\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm curious about the ties the era have to those other Eras, specially To the Strongest. Can you (or someone else) help me out? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Fall of Isireion&quot; is a sort of historical sequel to &quot;To the Strongest&quot;. Overt references are made to Alexander the Great and his passing and how everyone afterwards are trying to chase after his legacy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-07T13:00:27-08:00","id":1183359,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1066792-dark-eras-fall-of-isireion-discussion?p=1183356#post1183356\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Fall of Isireion&quot; is a sort of historical sequel to &quot;To the Strongest&quot;. Overt references are made to Alexander the Great and his passing and how everyone afterwards are trying to chase after his legacy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you. I thought there were more direct references and I was curious. I'm planning on starting a To the Strongest campaign, and tie in a trilogy of campaigns with Seven Wonders and Fall of Isireion. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/196-max-deltree","name":"Max Deltree","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar196_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"178"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-04T04:30:51-07:00","id":1214990,"title":"","content":"Cannibal Hymn, Iserion and To The Strongest were all done by me in part so I was able to create those connections.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Writer, Game Designer, Pro since 99.<br /> <br /> Thoughts at <a href=\"http://mobunited.com\" target=\"_blank\">mobunited.com</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/164-malcolm","name":"Malcolm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar164_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-04T14:58:27-07:00","id":1215243,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1066792-dark-eras-fall-of-isireion-discussion?p=1092399#post1092399\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have a question about Open Rites and Open Rite Mastery:<br /> <br /> Do you buy Open Rite Mastery for <i>each </i>open rite or once bought it applies to every open rite you can perform?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's each open Rite. And instances of a given type can be counted as a separate open Rite for the purpose of Open Rite Mastery.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}